shape theory.emergence : theory.contact.mutual, theory.coherence.law1 {
  type: definition
  layer: 0
  """
// Section 6 (Emergence).
// When shapes are in mutual contact, the contact produces coupling:
// each shape's character enters the other's transformation. The
// coupled system is itself a shape. This is emergence: contact
// produces new shapes with their own structure and character.
//
// Emergence is primarily a Law 1 phenomenon: stable reference
// between shapes in contact requires mutual coherence, and this
// mutual coherence requirement is what produces the emergent shape.
// Law 2 constrains what structure the emergent shape can have.
// Law 3 determines what happens when coupled shapes are incompatible.
//
// Derives from: theory.contact.mutual (emergence requires mutual contact),
//               theory.coherence.law1 (stable reference produces it)
  """
}
